
Pieces I've read/seen that left an impression or that I would recommend to anyone. The list is a mix of everything related to software engineering, from _people_ to _processes_ and uh, well, _*software*_.

- *[How to ask good questions](https://jvns.ca/blog/good-questions/)*
- *[The one ring problem: abstraction and our quest for power](https://www.tedinski.com/2018/01/30/the-one-ring-problem-abstraction-and-power.html)*
- *[You Might Be Better Off Without Pull Requests](https://hamvocke.com/blog/better-off-without-pull-requests/)*
- *[Value over replacement in software engineering](https://www.seangoedecke.com/value-over-replacement/)*

